    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1431">

                <pb facs="1799" n="1599" xml:id="pg1599"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–3045</note>
                <head>No. 1431<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Text Submitted by the Soviet
                        Delegation</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1431-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1945-08-01T23:59:59+03:00"
                            notBefore="1945-07-30T00:00:00+03:00">Undated</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Soviet Draft Translation</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Concerning the Transfer to the
                        Soviet Union of the City of koenigsberg and adjacent area</hi></p>
                <p>The Conference examined the proposal of the Soviet Government<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1431-f2"/> that prior to the final decision on territorial
                    questions at the peace settlement that the section of the western frontier of
                    the USSR adjacent to the Baltic Sea should pass from a point on the west bank of
                    the Gulf of Danzig to the east, north of Braunsberg–Goldap to the meeting point
                    of the frontiers of Lithuania, the Polish Republic, and East Prussia.</p>
                <p>The Conference agreed in principle with the proposal of the Soviet Government
                    concerning the transfer to the Soviet Union of the City of Koenigsberg and its
                    adjacent area.</p>
                <p>The President of the United States and the Prime Minister of Great Britain
                    declare that they will support this proposal at the forthcoming peace
                    conference.</p>
            </div>
